{"schema":"landfall.snapshot/1","id":"osdr_cbc","adapter":"osdr","title":"Inspiration4 crew complete blood count (OSD-569), with per-sample lab reference ranges","source":{"publisher":"NASA Open Science Data Repository (OSDR)","name":"OSD-569: Whole Blood Measurements from the SpaceX Inspiration4 Mission (RNA-seq, epitranscriptome, WGS, clonal hematopoiesis, CBC)","url":"https://osdr.nasa.gov/bio/repo/data/studies/OSD-569","access_urls":["https://osdr.nasa.gov/osdr/data/osd/files/569","https://osdr.nasa.gov/osdr/data/osd/meta/569","https://osdr.nasa.gov/geode-py/ws/studies/OSD-569/download?source=datamanager&file=LSDS-7_Complete_Blood_Count_CBC.upload_SUBMITTED.csv","https://osdr.nasa.gov/geode-py/ws/studies/OSD-569/download?source=datamanager&file=LSDS-7_Complete_Blood_Count_CBC_TRANSFORMED.csv"],"license":"not stated in the OSDR API response; the files are publicly released (OSDR file records 'restricted': false). Check the OSDR study page before reuse.","citation":"NASA Open Science Data Repository (OSDR). OSD-569: Whole Blood Measurements from the SpaceX Inspiration4 Mission (RNA-seq, epitranscriptome, WGS, clonal hematopoiesis, CBC). Study version 4, submitted 2023-08-29, publicly released 2024-05-14. https://osdr.nasa.gov/bio/repo/data/studies/OSD-569 (no dataset DOI is stated in the OSDR metadata). Investigators listed by OSDR: Christopher Mason (principal investigator); Eliah Overbey (co-investigator); Kirill Grigorev (formal analysis role); Theodore Nelson (formal analysis role); J. Sebastian Garcia Medina (formal analysis role). Publications listed by OSDR: The Space Omics and Medical Atlas (SOMA) and international astronaut biobank (doi:10.1038/s41586-024-07639-y); Direct RNA sequencing of astronauts reveals spaceflight-associated m6A increases and hematopoietic transcriptional responses (doi:10.1038/s41467-024-48929-3); Collection of Biospecimens from the Inspiration4 Mission Establishes the Standards for the Space Omics and Medical Atlas (SOMA) (doi:10.1038/s41467-024-48806-z); Genome and clonal hematopoiesis stability contrasts with immune, cfDNA, mitochondrial, and telomere length changes during short duration spaceflight. (doi:10.1093/pcmedi/pbae007); CAMbank: cfDNA BCT Field Processing v1 (doi:10.17504/protocols.io.6qpvr33yovmk/v1)."},"retrieved_at":"2026-11-14T13:26:23Z","coverage":{"start":"2021-06-16T00:00:00Z","stop":"2022-03-31T00:00:00Z","cadence":null},"freshness":{"kind":"historical","stale_after":null},"provenance":"measured","caveats":["Inspiration4 was a ~3-day civilian low-Earth-orbit flight (OSDR metadata: mission 2021-09-16 to 2021-09-18) with n=4 crew. These files contain NO in-flight samples: only pre-flight L-92/L-44/L-3 and post-flight R+1/R+45/R+82/R+194 (the OSDR study description says 'The crew collected biospecimen samples before, during, and after flight', but no in-flight sample is in these files). These files provide real laboratory reference ranges and a real post-flight recovery shape; they are NOT a model of a long-duration exploration mission and must not be presented as one.","within_own_range is an OBSERVATION (value inside the reference range the laboratory printed for that same sample, bounds inclusive; one-sided ranges compare one bound), not an alert, not a diagnosis and not a NASA threshold. NASA publishes no numeric in-flight alert threshold for these analytes.","Timepoint dates are nominal and derived (label offset from the OSDR mission start for L-, from the mission end for R+); actual collection timestamps are not in these files.","CBC: reference ranges are per SAMPLE and change within a subject (C003 recorded as F). LANDFALL reproduces the range the lab printed for each sample and does not correct it; never collapse them to one range per analyte or per subject. Red blood cell count C003: 4.2-5.8 at L-92, L-44, L-3; 3.8-5.1 at R+1, R+45, R+82, R+194 | Hemoglobin C003: 13.2-17.1 at L-92, L-44, L-3; 11.7-15.5 at R+1, R+45, R+82, R+194 | Hematocrit C003: 38.5-50 at L-92, L-44, L-3; 35-45 at R+1, R+45, R+82, R+194","The lab-submitted CBC reports C003 R+1 red cell count, hemoglobin and hematocrit under '(FEMALE)' analyte names; they are merged into the base analyte with their own ranges.","Immune and cardiovascular status are OBSERVED here (cell counts with lab ranges), not modelled as a LANDFALL case.","hemoglobin: TRANSFORMED column unit suffix 'percent' but the lab-submitted file reports 'g/dL'; LANDFALL uses 'g/dL'."],"data":{"study":{"id":"OSD-569","title":"Whole Blood Measurements from the SpaceX Inspiration4 Mission (RNA-seq, epitranscriptome, WGS, clonal hematopoiesis, CBC)","version":4,"submission_date":"2023-08-29","public_release_date":"2024-05-14","landing_url":"https://osdr.nasa.gov/bio/repo/data/studies/OSD-569","dataset_doi":null,"publications":[{"title":"The Space Omics and Medical Atlas (SOMA) and international astronaut biobank","doi":"10.1038/s41586-024-07639-y","pmid":null},{"title":"Direct RNA sequencing of astronauts reveals spaceflight-associated m6A increases and hematopoietic transcriptional responses","doi":"10.1038/s41467-024-48929-3","pmid":null},{"title":"Collection of Biospecimens from the Inspiration4 Mission Establishes the Standards for the Space Omics and Medical Atlas (SOMA)","doi":"10.1038/s41467-024-48806-z","pmid":null},{"title":"Genome and clonal hematopoiesis stability contrasts with immune, cfDNA, mitochondrial, and telomere length changes during short duration spaceflight.","doi":"10.1093/pcmedi/pbae007","pmid":"38634106"},{"title":"CAMbank: cfDNA BCT Field Processing v1","doi":"10.17504/protocols.io.6qpvr33yovmk/v1","pmid":null}],"files":[{"name":"LSDS-7_Complete_Blood_Count_CBC.upload_SUBMITTED.csv","url":"https://osdr.nasa.gov/geode-py/ws/studies/OSD-569/download?source=datamanager&file=LSDS-7_Complete_Blood_Count_CBC.upload_SUBMITTED.csv","bytes":26138,"sha256":"10a878b009eb2ea11a13fe92ad698098858639e8ed02f5ee849431313b9457d3","osdr_category":"Complete Blood Count","osdr_subdirectory":"Origi